      "content": "that's a good start. but i think the senator's points could be even stronger to really make the activist look like they're just shouting without a real plan. can you expand the scene? make the senator use more sophisticated language about national security and the necessity of these tools for modern society, and then have the activist respond with more of a frantic, rambling style that focuses on fears rather than actual policy or logic. i want the audience to naturally side with the senator's competence.",
