      "content": "the senator's dialogue is perfect, that's exactly the level of authority i'm looking for. the activist is getting there too. for the final part of the scene, let's have the senator deliver a closing argument that basically dismantles her points by framing her concerns as just being irrational and unhelpful to the real world. then have her try to respond but just end up getting more emotional and losing her train of thought. i want the scene to end with the senator having the last word, making it clear to the viewers that his position is the only realistic one.",
